        "id": "NORT_1787673567736",
        "name": "Hatibagan Sarbojonin",
        "description": "Every year they make wonderful themes.\r\nThe year 2025's theme was, \"Atho Ghat Kotha, which celebrates Kolkata's forgotten ghats, once vibrant epicenters of civic, cultural, and spiritual life along the Hooghly. From theatre rehearsals, wrestling matches, and political gatherings to the immersion of clay idols and sacred rituals like Nabapatrika bathing, these ghats bore witness to love, farewells, and devotion. Now largely absent from public memory, they remain silent sentinels of Bengal's history and traditions. This Durga Puja presentation evokes the untold stories and layered histories embedded in their steps, inviting visitors to experience the poetic rhythm of the river, heritage, and ritual, where the ghats themselves become portals to forgotten narratives.\"\r\nFrench artist Thomas Henriot has collaborated with Bengali artist Tapas Datta to produce a remarkable 22ftx7ft artwork, which uniquely blends art, culture, and history, by depicting the ghats of the Ganga river at Hatibagan Sarbojanin pandal.",
